# Project Standards

Work incrementally in small vertical slices.

Priorities:
- Keep the app runnable after every change.
- Prefer one complete working flow over many unfinished features.
- Avoid overengineering and premature abstractions.
- Do not rewrite unrelated code.
- Keep files small, cohesive, and easy to review.
- Use clear names for modules, services, DTOs, entities, and methods.
- Controllers should stay thin.
- Business logic belongs in services.
- Validate all incoming API input.
- Return informative errors.
- Prefer simple, production-oriented solutions.
- Do not add features that are not required unless core requirements are stable.